%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
title: a2.1 Residents, family and staff
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Seven stakeholders shape how social introductions unfold in the care home. A resident with dementia (ST-01), often new to the facility or isolated in their bedroom, meets, converses with, and invites a fellow resident (ST-02). Three stakeholders help broker that connection: the relative, who arranges the move and shares biographical history (ST-03); the care worker, who welcomes newcomers, supports daily meetings, and handles sensitive questions (ST-04); and the activity coordinator, who records life stories, reviews matches, and arranges seating (ST-05). Medical and therapy staff assess cognitive and clinical suitability (ST-06), while care home management oversees admissions, staffing, and data protection (ST-07). All share a commitment to the resident's well-being and trust, while balancing social encouragement against personal autonomy and privacy.

= Stakeholder - Resident with dementia [ST-01] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-01
|Name|Resident with dementia
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional; derived from SA-01 to SA-04 through group reasoning.
|Type|Direct - moves into the home, converses with the System, meets peers, and extends or considers invitations
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-06 Social connectedness (high) - genuine company, conversation, and friendship with peers
* HV-02 Dignity (high) - being spoken to as an adult, without memory slips being exposed or patronised
* HV-08 Truthfulness (high) - honest answers from a trusted person regarding painful topics such as why they live here or who has passed away
* HV-01 Autonomy (high) - deciding for oneself whom to meet, when to socialise, and when to stay in one's room
* HV-03 Privacy (high) - keeping personal secrets and controlling what biographical facts are shared with others
* HV-07 Identity (high) - being known through one's own history, former trade, interests, and words
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - calm, enjoyable days with something to look forward to
* HV-04 Safety (high) - feeling secure and unthreatened in shared spaces and activities
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Arrives knowing nobody in the facility. Meets and spends time with ST-02. Relatives (ST-03) help provide biographical history and consent. Welcomed and supported by ST-04 and ST-05. Cognitive and clinical needs assessed by ST-06.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-01 to SA-04; holds → HV-01 to HV-08; appears-in → PS-01 to PS-04; elaborated-as → HP-01, HP-02 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Fellow resident [ST-02] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-02
|Name|Fellow resident
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional; derived from SA-01, SA-03, and SA-04 through group reasoning.
|Type|Direct - interacts with the System, accepts or declines introductions, and talks with ST-01 (often also living with mild to moderate dementia)
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-06 Social connectedness (high) - finding a compatible peer to talk and spend time with
* HV-01 Autonomy (high) - freedom to decline an introduction or leave a conversation without pressure
* HV-03 Privacy (high) - control over their own personal history and private room time
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - calm, pleasant company without agitation or social strain
* HV-02 Dignity (medium) - being treated as a peer rather than an obligation
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Encounters ST-01 in communal rooms or through introductions brokered by ST-04, ST-05, or the System. Has their own family (ST-03) and care plan.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-03, SA-04; supports → SA-01; holds → HV-01 to HV-03, HV-05, HV-06; appears-in → PS-01, PS-03, PS-04; elaborated-as → HP-01, HP-02 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Relative [ST-03] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-03
|Name|Relative
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional; derived from SA-01 to SA-04 through group reasoning.
|Type|Indirect - arranges the admission, contributes to the life story, agrees on how sensitive topics are handled, and provides legal representative consent where needed
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-06 Social connectedness (high) - wanting their relative to have companionship and friends in the home
* HV-08 Truthfulness (high) - expecting staff and systems not to deceive their relative
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - seeing their relative settle in, stay engaged, and avoid isolation
* HV-07 Identity (high) - having their relative's life history known and respected
* HV-03 Privacy (low) - willing to share personal details with staff to help their relative settle, sometimes more freely than the resident themselves would choose
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Family member of ST-01. Shares biographical background with ST-05 and agrees with ST-04 on who should answer painful questions.

== Graph edges ==

supports → SA-01 to SA-04; holds → HV-03, HV-05 to HV-08; appears-in → PS-01, PS-03.

= Stakeholder - Care worker [ST-04] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-04
|Name|Care worker
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional; derived from SA-01 to SA-04 through group reasoning.
|Type|Direct - welcomes newcomers, brings matched residents together in common areas, supports informal meetings, and answers sensitive questions
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-04 Safety (high) - keeping residents physically and emotionally safe during daily routines
* HV-08 Truthfulness (high) - giving honest, compassionate answers and keeping confidences
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - seeing residents calm, comfortable, and free from agitation
* HV-06 Social connectedness (medium) - helping residents get to know one another when shift time allows
* HV-03 Privacy (medium) - respecting residents' private space and refusing workplace surveillance of staff
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Acts as the trusted person for sensitive questions as agreed with ST-03. Shares day-to-day observations with ST-05 about which residents get along, and follows clinical guidance from ST-06.

== Graph edges ==

supports → SA-01 to SA-04; holds → HV-03 to HV-06, HV-08; appears-in → PS-01 to PS-03; elaborated-as → HP-03 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Activity coordinator [ST-05] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-05
|Name|Activity coordinator
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional; derived from SA-01 to SA-04 through group reasoning.
|Type|Direct - conducts life-story interviews, manages the relationship map, reviews compatibility matches, and facilitates communal activities
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-06 Social connectedness (high) - fostering friendships and using shared activities to ease first contact
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - keeping residents engaged and content
* HV-07 Identity (high) - grounding activities and introductions in each resident's life story
* HV-03 Privacy (high) - safeguarding the biographical histories entrusted to them
* HV-01 Autonomy (medium) - ensuring residents choose which invitations and activities to accept
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Records life stories with ST-01 and ST-03. Coordinates introductions and seating with ST-04. Employed by ST-07.

== Graph edges ==

supports → SA-01 to SA-04; holds → HV-01, HV-03, HV-05 to HV-07; appears-in → PS-02.

= Stakeholder - Medical and therapy staff [ST-06] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-06
|Name|Medical and therapy staff (physician, nurse, physiotherapist, psychologist)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional; derived from SA-01 and SA-04 through group reasoning.
|Type|Indirect - assess cognitive status, behavioural symptoms, and mobility, and communicate clinical diagnoses
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-04 Safety (high) - preventing physical harm, falls, and acute behavioural distress
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - supporting mood, cognitive stimulation, and healthy daily activity
* HV-08 Truthfulness (high) - ensuring clinical diagnoses and medical realities are communicated properly
* HV-03 Privacy (medium) - upholding medical confidentiality
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Assess ST-01 and ST-02 and advise ST-04 and ST-05 on clinical or mobility boundaries. Serve as the trusted authority for medical questions.

== Graph edges ==

supports → SA-01, SA-04; holds → HV-03 to HV-05, HV-08.

= Stakeholder - Care home management [ST-07] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-07
|Name|Care home management
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional; derived from SA-01 and SA-04 through group reasoning.
|Type|Indirect - oversees admissions, staffing, facility safety, and data protection, and decides on deploying the System
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-04 Safety (high) - institutional responsibility for resident safety and duty of care
* HV-03 Privacy (high) - compliance with GDPR and health-data protection standards
* HV-05 Well-being (medium) - overall quality of residential care and family satisfaction
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Employs ST-04 and ST-05, admits ST-01, and governs facility policies and local data infrastructure.

== Graph edges ==

governs → SA-01 (admissions), SA-04 (staffing and communal spaces), System data; holds → HV-03 to HV-05.

